==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|EN-AU ck1 creepy-crawly.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Etymology 1===

====Noun====
{{en-noun|head=[[creepy]]-[[crawly]]}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} Any small [[crawling]] [[animal]] such as a [[spider]], [[insect]] or [[worm]] that is [[unpleasant]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1919|title=Brother Bosch: An Airman's Escape from Germany|author=Gerald Featherstone Knight|url=https://www.gutenberg.org/files/27229/27229-h/27229-h.htm|passage=Mattresses were either spring or made of old straw, and sometimes contained little '''creepy-crawlies'''.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=Tracy McVeigh|url=http://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2013/mar/02/insects-next-food-source|title=Insects could be the planet's next food source… even if that gives you the creeps|date=2013-03-02|work=The Observer|passage=Many experts believe there is a clear environmental benefit to humans eating '''creepy-crawlies'''.}}

